                  <msItem>
                     <title>Ricardus Armachanus, Sermones, etc.</title>
                     <note type="MLGB3_generalNotes">The flyleaves, part of an office of St Guthlac,
                        s. xii in., are kept separately as MS. D.1.25a. Six in number, they come
                        partly from the beginning (fol. 1, 2 and 6) and partly from the end (fol.
                        3--5) of MS. 370, as wormholes show. They contain inter alia part of an
                        office for St Guthlac, s. xii in.</note>
                     <note type="MLGB3_generalNotes">There is no direct evidenc that fol. 93and
                        following have any original connection with fol. 1-92.</note>
                  </msItem>
